# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your own keys.
# .env itself is gitignored — keys never enter the repo or the browser.
# Fill in as many providers as you like; the app uses whichever exist,
# and the model picker disables providers without a key.
GROQ_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# --- Server & deployment (all optional for local runs) ---
# Django secret key. Unset locally = a built-in dev fallback is used;
# with KAI_PRODUCTION=1 the app REFUSES to boot without a real one.
# SECRET_KEY=
# Postgres connection string (e.g. Neon). Unset = local SQLite file.
# DATABASE_URL=
# This deployment's own public URL, e.g. https://kai-ai-02i0.onrender.com
# Production derives ALLOWED_HOSTS and CSRF-trusted origins from it.
# (Some platforms expose the same value as SITE_URL — either works.)
# APP_URL=
# Comma-separated host allowlist override; normally unnecessary —
# APP_URL above covers the deployed case.
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# Django debug: "0"/"false" = off. Local default is on; the deployed
# service sets it to False (render.yaml).
# DEBUG=
# Bootstrap secret for first-owner setup: /api/auth/setup/ requires
# this token (and only works while zero users exist). Use a long
# random value. Without it, web setup is disabled and the owner is
# created with `python manage.py createsuperuser` instead. After the
# owner exists the token is useless and can be removed.
# KAI_SETUP_TOKEN=
# Optional: pin one provider (groq / openrouter / nvidia / deepseek /
# gemini) and disable cross-provider fallback.
# AI_PROVIDER=
# Optional: folder the coding agent's FILE tools may read/write in.
# Defaults to the project's agent_workspace/ directory. The file tools cannot escape
# this folder — but code EXECUTED by run_command runs with the server
# process's privileges, so execution is a separate, stricter switch:
# KAI_WORKSPACE=
# Command execution kill switch (Phase 1). Execution only happens
# when this is exactly "1". NEVER set it on a public deployment —
# a restricted subprocess is not a true sandbox.
# KAI_CODING_ENABLED=
# Deployed services set this to "1" (render.yaml does): production
# then requires a real SECRET_KEY and turns on secure cookies/HSTS.
# KAI_PRODUCTION=
